765148197,"type":"genre","name":"dance","n":1},{"id":87625349211221,"type":"genre","name":"electronic","n":1},{"id":42409133203490,"type":"genre","name":"Euro House","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":132218155550361,"name":"Techno y trance de los noventa","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1990,"end":2001,"desc":"El techno y el house tardan una década en dominar el baile, pero luego se extienden como la pólvora y la diferencia entre ambos se difumina. Bélgica (Lords Of Acid), Francia (Laurent Garnier), Japón (Ken Ishii); Alemania tiene la escena más variada: Sven Väth inventa el trance de Frankfurt, Air Liquide el techno psicodélico de Colonia, La Bouche, L@n. Jimi Tenor, Ace Of Base, Aqua; en Australia, David Thrussell (Snog, Black Lung, Soma). EE UU, cuna del techno, es derivativo: Deee-Lite, Crystal Method, Jeff Mills (Underground Resistance), BT (el «epic house»), Wod, y San Francisco con su psicodelia electrónica (Hardkiss, Freaky Chakra). En Gran Bretaña, EMF, Utah Saints, Carter USM y el «Goa trance» de Paul Oakenfold (Paul Van Dyk, ATB).","color":"#facc15","family":"Soul, funk, disco, hip hop y baile","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#techno-90s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":18130386806746,"artist":"Aqua","artist_id":213012516441151,"title":"Aquarium","year":1997,"ess":0,"yt":"OG0AvwM_QAI","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Techno y trance de los noventa","scene_id":132218155550361,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#techno-90s","chapters":["Sección 6.9"],"pages":[[1,261,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":68,"text":"…every other member of Tangerine Dream launched a solo career, but noone was as successful as Schulze. Romance '76 (1976), by Peter Baumann (1) and Aqua (1974), by Edgar Froese (1), were probably the best of the solo works of the others, while Chris Franke (1) would not release a significant work…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":261,"text":"…in a clearly Abba-derived fashion, as Ace Of Base did with All That She Wants (1992) and Beautiful Life (1995), or in an ironic synth-pop style, as Aqua (1) did on the exuberant Aquarium (1997). Australia's most creative techno musician was perhaps David Thrussell, who evolved from the naive techno…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Bavarian Eurodance Act (Late 1990s)","body":"Aqua was a band that emerged from Northern Europe (specifically Norway, Sweden, or Denmark) and became associated with the Bavarian Eurodance subgenre. They were known for embodying the genre's most saccharine, \"cardboard,\" and exaggerated phase in the late 1990s. \"...con bandas como Aqua...\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"La gran mentira detrás del Eurodance","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_F34L8wfrdo"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":3960969789830,"type":"song","name":"Barbie Girl","work_year":1997,"list_id":46818025098002,"list":"Billboard Year-End 1997","src":"singles","rank":94,"year":1997,"note":"","yt":"ZyhrYis509A","scaruffi":null},{"id":3960969789830,"type":"song","name":"Barbie Girl","work_year":1997,"list_id":132335824845498,"list":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","src":"charts","rank":94,"year":1997,"note":null,"yt":"ZyhrYis509A","scaruffi":null},{"id":3960969789830,"type":"song","name":"Barbie Girl","work_year":1997,"list_id":75028305851756,"list":"Los 40 nº1 · 1997","src":"singles","rank":49,"year":1997,"note":"","yt":"ZyhrYis509A","scaruffi":null},{"id":18130386806746,"type":"album","name":"Aquarium","list_id":4389278164509,"list":"Music Genre Tree","src":"musthear","rank":64,"year":1997,"note":null,"yt":"GoE3YNAaoYk","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":18130386806746,"type":"album","name":"Aquariu